# Guest data and generated invitation messages.
#
# `data/guests.csv` is a list of real people — names, households, email
# addresses. `out/links.csv` carries their invite codes, which are the only thing
# standing between that list and anyone who guesses one. Neither belongs in git.
# The .example.csv beside them is the template and *is* tracked.
#
# Ignoring `/data/*` rather than `/data/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so excluding the directory itself would make the negation below
# unreachable.
/data/*
!/data/guests.example.csv
/out/

# Firebase service-account keys. Firebase names them
# `<project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json`, so match on the shape rather than the
# exact name.
*service*account*.json
*service-account*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
